+# Registration Interface
+
+Entry point for FlaskBB user self-registration. It is backed by the registered
+`register_user` Pipeline route and does not re-implement Service logic.
+
+## Adapter
+
+- Manifest: `interfaces/registration/interface.json` (name `registration`, kind `web`)
+- Adapter: `interfaces/registration/adapter.py`, class `RegistrationAdapter`
+- Routes: `register_user` (`pipelines/registration.py`)
+- Host compatibility: `flaskbb.auth.services.registration.RegistrationService`
+  re-exports this adapter, so FlaskBB's registration factory and views keep working.
+
+## No standalone launcher
+
+This interface is hosted by FlaskBB. `start()` accepts a `RegistrationEnvelope`
+and runs the registered route; `register(user_info)` is the host-facing entry
+that binds FlaskBB's plugin manager, `User` model and SQLAlchemy session, then
+delegates to the same route. The adapter's `smoke_payloads()` returns a
+non-destructive sample (`envelope: None`) used only for declaration checks.
+
+## Checks
+
+From the project root:
+
+```
+python -m ai_pod_cli interface --project-root . smoke registration
+python -m ai_pod_cli interface --project-root . run registration --payload '{"envelope": null}'
+python -m pytest -o addopts='' tests/interfaces/test_registration_adapter.py -q
+python -m pytest -o addopts='' tests -q
+```
+
+The `run` CLI, like `start`, needs a FlaskBB application context and bound
+registration resources, so end-to-end behavior is covered by
+`tests/interfaces/test_registration_adapter.py` and the host registration tests
+rather than by a standalone server process.
